cff-version: 1.2.0
title: An enzyme-resolved dataset linking drug interaction mechanisms to clinical severity grades
message: Cite this repository review snapshot; DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23169653 is reserved for an unpublished Zenodo draft and is not a published dataset DOI.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Noor
    given-names: Adeeb
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8251-1853
    affiliation: Department of Information Technology, Faculty of Computing and Information Technology, King Abdulaziz University, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia
abstract: >-
  Author-derived review snapshot of 1900 drug pairs, 240 drugs and 35 source
  protein labels. DDInter clinical grades are reconstructed locally from the
  user's authorised download. Original D3 rule logic is recovered; complete
  graph-to-current-record reconstruction remains unresolved. All 35 protein
  accessions have a frozen current human gene audit; two source symbol conflicts
  are resolved separately while raw annotations are preserved.
  Includes exploratory statistics, recovered descriptive author-reference membership
  comparisons, reported KEGG aggregates and a self-contained browser. The incomplete
  selected phenotype layer is withdrawn. Original D3 rule logic is recovered; exact
  full graph-to-current-record identity remains unresolved.
keywords:
  - drug-drug interactions
  - cytochrome P450
  - drug transporters
  - DDInter
  - data provenance
repository-code: https://github.com/adeebnoor/ddi-enzyme-severity-resource
url: https://github.com/adeebnoor/ddi-enzyme-severity-resource
version: 2.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
